  "configuration_id": "config_039",
  "reason": "The dominant finding across all 5 completed experiments is that the scvi_n200 RNA encoder (config_008, 70.6% acc) dramatically outperforms scgpt (~52-54%), making it the clear backbone to build on. Among scgpt experiments, avgpool+weighted and ViT-L were the best-performing aggregation/fusion/image-encoder choices, which is exactly the recipe in config_008. The remaining untested variation within this 'best-of-each' family is the aggregation method: transformer vs. avgpool. With scvi_n200's richer learned latent space, transformer-based cross-profile aggregation may capture interactions that simple averaging misses (the scgpt evidence for avgpool>transformer was only ~2 pts and may not transfer to a different feature space). config_039 (scvi_n200 + ViT-L + transformer + weighted) keeps the two strongest factors and the best fusion while testing this one architectural question. Expected cost is moderate (~4-5 GPU hours, comparable to config_008's 4.82 h, with a small increase from transformer attention). This is the highest-value single experiment: if it beats 70.6%, we have a new best; if it matches or falls slightly short, we confirm avgpool is optimal and can spend remaining budget on other directions (e.g., singleprofile or PCA variants) with confidence."
}

